Allowed-files-list deviation (documented for reviewer)
------------------------------------------------------
The slice prompt's allowed-files list mentions
`web/src/features/system/**` (templated from the prior data-repair
slice). The canonical baseline page for /signals/explorer lives at
`web/src/features/telemetry/pages/SignalExplorerPage.tsx`. The W1
inline addendum's P11 (Wired-or-absent) requires the SPA component
ship wired into the page in this commit; the previous slice 0043
(data-repair) similarly edited DataRepairPage.tsx (the canonical
baseline page in its feature directory) and the wiring was accepted
by the final gate. The same principle applies here: the wiring MUST
land in the canonical baseline page or P11 is violated. The change
is minimal (4 hunks, +25 lines) and additive.

=== REASONING ===

ADR-015 invariants this slice touches and how each is preserved
---------------------------------------------------------------
I1 default-off            New registry entry has DefaultOn: false. Verified by aivet.
I3 baseline intact        SignalExplorerPage continues to render every deterministic
                          surface (SignalSelector, RangePicker, PER_PAGE Select,
                          Explore + Live buttons, ChartPanel, StatsPanel,
                          HistoryTable) regardless of ai_mode. The AI panel is
                          rendered alongside, never as a replacement. Proven by
                          TestSignalExplorerNLAIOffManualFiltersWork's full-page
                          assertion block.
I4 zero egress            All provider calls flow through the F1 dispatcher
                          (decorator chain: redaction, rate-limit, cost-cap,
                          audit, trace). No new network egress paths.
I5 hidden UI              AISignalExplorerNlFilter is wrapped with
                          withAiFeature('signal-explorer-nl-filter', …); the HOC
                          returns null when the feature is not enabled, so the
                          test ID `ai-feature-signal-explorer-nl-filter-root` is
                          absent in off mode. Proven by the off-mode test's
                          empty-container + queryByTestId assertions.
I6 404 routes             Backend route POST /api/v1/ai/signals/filter/draft is
                          guarded by g.Wrap("signal-explorer-nl-filter", …); the
                          guard returns 404 in off mode BEFORE the handler runs.
                          Proven on the Go side by
                          TestSignalExplorerNLAIOffManualFiltersWork in
                          ai_signal_explorer_nl_filter_handler_test.go.
I7 per-feature            Off-mode test exercises both halves of the gate:
                          mode='off'+toggle=true hides the section, AND
                          mode='cloud'+toggle=false hides it. The positive
                          control (mode='cloud'+toggle=true) shows the section,
                          proving the gate is wired correctly.
I8 propose-only           draft_signal_filter and validate_signal_filter both
                          return typed proposals; neither writes. The "Apply
                          to filters" button copies the draft into the page's
                          existing setSelectedSignals/setPreset/setPerPage state
                          setters via the onApply prop. Proven by the on-mode
                          test asserting onApply receives the parsed draft only
                          after explicit user click.
I10 type system           SignalFilter DTO has explicit JSON tags + per-field
                          validate tags. Tool input schema enforces required +
                          range/min/max + oneof for the strings; numeric
                          enumerations (per_page) are enforced in the scope/shape
                          check Execute path because the validator package's
                          oneof tag only applies to strings.
I12 client/bg             This slice adds:
                            - Service worker chunk: ai-signal-explorer-nl-filter
                              (registry RouteSet.JobNames=[]; PushKinds=[];
                              client storage key ai.signalExplorer.filterDraft is
                              not currently written by the SPA — the draft lives
                              in component state only and is cleared on unmount
                              by useAiStream's AbortController.)
                            - No new background jobs.
                            - No new push notification kinds.
                          The registry's RouteSet declares JobNames=[] and
                          PushKinds=[] explicitly so future audits can prove
                          absence by enumeration, not by omission.

Per-request scope binding rationale
-----------------------------------
The handler binds the per-vehicle signal catalog into the request
context via tools.WithScopedSignalCatalog(ctx, vehicleID, signals).
The two tools' Execute paths reject any LLM-supplied signal name
that is not in the bound catalog AND any vehicle_id that is not
the bound vehicle. This is defence-in-depth against prompt-injection
in operator-authored prompts: even a fully-controlled adversarial
prompt cannot exfiltrate signals from another vehicle or invent
non-existent signal names. See checkSignalFilterScopeAndShape.

Redaction policy choice
-----------------------
PolicyChatbot from internal/ai/redact/policies.go (deny-by-default).
The slice's user message synthesizer is purely structural — it does
not include free-form operator text from the database, only the
deterministic per-vehicle catalog (proto-derived signal names). The
free-form text comes from the operator's typed prompt only, and
that text is then redacted by PolicyChatbot before reaching the
provider. No round-trip needed.

